    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1839">

                <pb facs="1471" n="1355" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg1355"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 033.1100 K77/221.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister of Venezuela to
                        the Assistant Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of Venezuela</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-02-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 14, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Wilson</hi>: I have read with the
                    greatest interest your obliging and welcome note of yesterday<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d1839-f1"/> by which you impart to me the good news that by
                    direction of His Excellency the President of United States the honorable
                    Secretary of State. Mr. Knox, will visit Venezuela [etc.].</p>
                <p>The idea is most praiseworthy and it affords me very great pleasure to inform you
                    that I have received cablegrams from the President of Venezuela, General Gómez,
                    and the Ministry of Foreign Relations instructing me to express to the
                    Department of State the delight with which the announcement of the visit was
                    received in Venezuela.</p>
                <p>The President of Venezuela, as well as the whole Government, and the city of
                    Caracas, are even now making preparations to receive their distinguished guest
                    with all the regard and attentions that are due to him.</p>
                <p>I beg you to inform His Excellency the President of the United States and the
                    Honorable Mr. Knox.</p>
                <p>Wishing to know in due time the exact date of the Secretary of State’s visit to
                    Venezuela, and also wishing that he may stay in Venezuela as many days as
                    possible, which will give my country great satisfaction,</p>
                <p>I renew to you [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">F. Ezequiel Rojas.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
